A relative `--target` is defined against the workdir, so it implies no workdir of its own even when
its tail matches the declared `artifact:` — deriving one would re-anchor the path under itself. The
moved file lands under the invocation directory and the hooks run there.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-hooks
title: Hooks
summary: Hook-bearing fixture for playbook-transition.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  only: []

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: noted
            when: the environment is recorded
            hooks: ["script env-note"]
      noted: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/only/prompt.md --
